WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.057 --> 00:00:03.890
- "To All The Boys I Loved
Before" blew up in 2018.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:04.723
- Yeah.

00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:05.900
- So how pumped are you for the sequel?

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.530
- I'm so stoked, it's like,
holding that secret in

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.060
that we were going to
make a second and a third

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.150
was the hardest thing
ever, but I'm so excited

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.350
and if you're a fan of "To All The Boys"

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.710
and you watched the first one,

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.376
I know that you're going
to love the second.

00:00:18.376 --> 00:00:19.209
- That's awesome.

00:00:19.209 --> 00:00:20.810
- And it's a really
wonderful, like you continue

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.700
to see her journey as
a young high schooler

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.950
trying to figure out
love and kind of balance

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.130
these new relationships,
so it's really, really fun.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:29.963
I loved it.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.720
- So the very first movie
you were in, what was it?

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.850
'Cause I'm super jealous, they don't know.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.343
- Oh. The very first movie I
was in was "X-Men: Apocalypse"

00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:38.484
back a little while ago.

00:00:38.484 --> 00:00:39.701
(crowd cheering)

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.510
- [Kelly] That was your first movie.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:42.530
- [Lana] Yeah.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.590
- Like usually, peoples'
first movie is like,

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.477
no one's heard of it.

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:47.100
(laughs)
That's X-Men.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.820
- It was like being just
thrown into the deep end.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.190
It was like sink or swim, right?

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.110
You're like "This is
gonna make or break me,

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.560
I might never work again."

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.720
But it was so amazing
and I was auditioning

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.343
as a second-semester
senior in high school.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.620
I knew I was in the running for it

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.410
and then I got a call from my
agents in the middle of class.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.930
And you're not supposed to have your phone

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.510
but I was like, "Yo".

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.440
'Cause if it's your
agent calling you pick up

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.380
no matter what, right?

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.426
- I don't, but go ahead.

00:01:15.426 --> 00:01:16.370
(crowd laughing)

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.040
- Well, that's good.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.070
- He's bothered.
(laughs)

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.170
- Right, right, right.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.020
And they were like, are you around anyone?

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.100
Can we tell you some news?

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.630
And I was like, "I'm around
everyone that I know".

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.100
So I ended up walking out of school

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.593
and I stood underneath
the great American flag.

00:01:33.995 --> 00:01:36.230
They told me that I had
booked it but that I couldn't

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.370
tell anyone until the
press release came out.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.970
So then I had to go back to freakin' class

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:41.803
being like,

00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:42.636
- And not freak out.

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:43.469
- "Oh my god, oh my god."

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:44.302
Yeah it was crazy.

00:01:44.302 --> 00:01:46.030
- That's an amazing first job.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.101
- Thank you.

00:01:47.101 --> 00:01:47.934
(cheering)

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.151
- I mean that's, that's killer.

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:55.151
- She's booking major
movies in high school

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.093
and I'm sweeping hair.

00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:58.940
(laughter)

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.638
- I was selling vacuums, so..

00:02:00.638 --> 00:02:02.343
(laughter)

00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:03.176
- You know,

00:02:03.176 --> 00:02:04.009
- You know, life.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:05.110
- You gotta do what you gotta do.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.610
So we're celebrating
"All the Feels February"

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.900
'cause it's Valentine's Day,
so you have anybody special?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.900
- I do, my boyfriend, Anthony,
the love of my life, yes.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.790
I don't know what we're gonna do.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.870
We're probably just gonna like,
stay at home and just eat,

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:20.824
like we always do.

00:02:20.824 --> 00:02:21.960
- [Kelly] That's the best date ever.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:22.936
Oh y'all are adorable.

00:02:22.936 --> 00:02:24.275
- [Lana] Oh, that's us.

00:02:24.275 --> 00:02:26.030
- [Kelly] Look at him in that hat, okay.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:26.863
- [Lana] Yeah.

00:02:26.863 --> 00:02:28.700
- [Kelly] Oh, look at this one.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.480
- [Lana] That's my puppy Emmy.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.110
- Emmy's adorable.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.061
I love your man but I love him more.

00:02:34.061 --> 00:02:34.894
- Yeah.

00:02:34.894 --> 00:02:35.727
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:35.727 --> 00:02:36.840
Or her, Emmy's a girl, right?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.673
- Yeah.

00:02:37.673 --> 00:02:39.600
- Yes, yes, yes, beauti-, how old?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.450
- We just celebrated her
one year, one years old

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.580
and one year being with us,

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.110
'cause we got her at like five weeks.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:50.540
She knows, she knows that
it's, that it's her one year

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.610
because we woke up, and I'm a little sick,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.290
so Anthony went and took
her out on her morning walk

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.970
and she pooped in the shape of a heart.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:02:59.803
(crowd laughing)

00:02:59.803 --> 00:03:02.940
Now, I would like to say
that I have a picture

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.070
of the said poop.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:04.947
- That's impressive.

00:03:04.947 --> 00:03:06.090
(laughter)

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:06.923
- And I can show it to you.

00:03:06.923 --> 00:03:08.035
- I feel challenged.

00:03:08.035 --> 00:03:09.730
(crowd laughing)

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.210
- I want you to know if you feel like,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.750
not the vibe, please look
away , but we have a photo.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.583
- You have a photo of the heart poop.

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:17.416
- Of the heart poop.

00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:18.862
- Okay, if you wanna look
at the heart poop, go ahead,

00:03:18.862 --> 00:03:20.460
if you don't, you know.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.137
I wanna look at the heart poop.

00:03:22.137 --> 00:03:25.887
(crowd laughing, applauding)

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.380
- That's actually very impressive.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.083
- Happy Valentine's Day, you guys.

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:36.230
- I mean, the only thing better is if she

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.022
just sat behind it and
was like, like after.

00:03:40.022 --> 00:03:42.390
So speaking of loved one's though,

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.190
you just went on a big family trip, right?

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.023
- I did.

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:45.856
- Yeah.

00:03:45.856 --> 00:03:48.410
- So I'm adopted from Vietnam and

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.100
my family and I have not
been able to go back yet

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.790
since I was adopted when I was a baby.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.850
So, just recently, we went back to Vietnam

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.750
and we found the
orphanage where my parents

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.750
got my brother and I and
we were able to go inside.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.870
The paint hasn't changed,
the curtains haven't changed.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.650
I was able to see where I
spent like the first, my first

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.120
couple of months on Earth as a baby.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.550
Being there with my family,

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.770
it was like full complete circle.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:21.770
I've never felt so just still,
and dropped-in and whole.

00:04:22.696 --> 00:04:23.554
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:23.554 --> 00:04:24.387
- It was amazing, so yeah..

00:04:24.387 --> 00:04:25.480
- Oh you are gonna Oprah me right now.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.120
Wow, that was really, oh my gosh,

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.120
I'm like, I'm gonna cry right now.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.680
- It was the best trip of my life

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.520
and I'm so happy that I was
able to finally do that,

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.353
'cause I've been wanting to do that.

00:04:35.353 --> 00:04:38.050
- Randomly enough, literally,
Vietnam is the first place

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.392
my little girl ever went outside America.

00:04:39.392 --> 00:04:40.225
- Really?

00:04:40.225 --> 00:04:41.470
- I did an event there, like years,

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.530
and it was right when River,

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.363
my little five year old,

00:04:43.363 --> 00:04:44.196
- [Lana] Yeah.

00:04:44.196 --> 00:04:45.150
- She was born, it was
the first place ever,

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.080
she was like three months old.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.980
- Did she like it?
- Well, who knows?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.656
- Sebastian, do you do any family trips?

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:51.674
Y'all big on that?

00:04:51.674 --> 00:04:53.944
- Yeah no, we didn't go to Vietnam.

00:04:53.944 --> 00:04:56.361
- No, no. Like any family trips?

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:58.309
- No we go to the zoo,
we went to the LA Zoo.

00:04:58.309 --> 00:04:59.476
- [Lana] Nice.

00:04:59.476 --> 00:05:00.309
- I love the zoo!

00:05:00.309 --> 00:05:02.060
- That's about as far as we got.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.490
But that's very bold to take a child

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.187
on a, that long of a
flight at three months.

00:05:06.187 --> 00:05:07.940
- I'll tell you what, I was terrified

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.400
'cause you didn't want all
those people to hate you.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.546
But like, she didn't cry once.

00:05:11.546 --> 00:05:12.379
- You know what I do,

00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:13.461
- She was the best.
- That's amazing.

00:05:13.461 --> 00:05:15.760
- You know what I do, which
I think is a nice touch?

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.370
I take a kid on a plane, I go around,

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.301
I pass out chocolates to everybody.

00:05:20.301 --> 00:05:21.134
- [Kelly] Like money.

00:05:21.134 --> 00:05:21.967
- [Lana] It's like bribery.

00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:24.510
- Yeah, so just in case the kid does cry,

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.090
people got a little sweet.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.180
- I know and it sucks though
because they look at you,

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.430
and they're like, "Can you do something?"

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.202
Like, do you think I
like what's happening?

00:05:31.202 --> 00:05:32.976
- Yeah. Do you think I want this?

00:05:32.976 --> 00:05:35.200
- Do you think I was
like, boy I hope my baby

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.550
loses it on the plane
and everyone hates me.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.840
You know, like what
are you supposed to do?

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.373
Anyway, Vietnam is a beautiful country,

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:42.360
- Yes, yes.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.820
- that was what I was trying to get to.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.983
- Yes. (laughter)

